{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e28ca108-d7c2-41a5-945f-b6dc26e9c965","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-98ed5b16017d5bd2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-1gijbjoi/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nConverts reconciliation error logging throughout the rhods-operator manager\nbinary from message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs.\nEvery reconciliation error log that currently embeds a resource name or\nnamespace in its message string (e.g. `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile\nDashboard 'example' in namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")`) is converted to\nstructured fields (`log.Error(err, \"reconciliation failed\", \"name\",\ndashboard.Name, \"namespace\", dashboard.Namespace, \"resourceKind\", \"Dashboard\")`).\nThe epic also migrates the DSCInitialization controller off its non-standard\nkey names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) onto the camelCase convention,\nadds `resourceKind` across all controller tiers, and adds a CI lint rule so\nnon-compliant log calls cannot be reintroduced. On completion, operators can\nquery rhods-operator manager error logs by resource name, namespace, and kind\nwithout parsing message text.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in manager-binary reconciliation error\n  paths and produce a per-tier coverage checklist (confirming the estimated\n  ~75% of calls that embed resource identity in message strings).\n- Convert every reconciliation error log in the manager binary that embeds\n  resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value\n  pairs using `name` and `namespace`.\n- Migrate the DSCInitialization controller from the non-standard key names\n  `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` to `name` and `namespace`.\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in:\n  - the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator,\n    Setup), where the kind is not implied by the controller name;\n  - the module controller and its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway,\n    KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator);\n  - the DataScienceCluster controller and the 8 component controllers\n    (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer,\n    TrainingOperator, TrustyAI) for cross-controller queryability;\n  - the DSCInitialization controller.\n- Apply `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` to error logs in all 15 action\n  files across the four tiers: 8 component action files\n  (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files\n  (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action\n  file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and 3\n  module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n- Handle cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization)\n  correctly: `name` and `resourceKind` present, `namespace` omitted or empty —\n  never a spurious value.\n- Add a CI lint/static-analysis rule to the repository that flags `log.Error`\n  calls embedding resource identity in message text or missing the required\n  structured fields, initially covering the manager binary paths.\n- Verify backwards compatibility: before/after log output comparison for a\n  sample reconciliation error; confirm the log consumer stack (Loki) ingests\n  both formats without configuration changes; coordinate with SRE/Support to\n  identify and update text-based alert rules that rely on changed message\n  strings.\n- Document the DSCI key-name migration in release notes with before/after\n  query examples, targeted at a single release transition.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Static analysis over the manager binary reports zero reconciliation-error\n  `log.Error` calls that embed resource name or namespace in the message text,\n  and the CI lint rule flags a deliberately non-compliant sample call in a test.\n- A codebase grep confirms no remaining `Request.Name` or `DSCInitialization`\n  structured key names in the DSCInitialization controller, and a unit test\n  asserting DSCI error logs contain `name` and `namespace` passes.\n- Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with\n  the correct value for all 5 service controllers, the module controller and\n  its 8 module handlers, the DataScienceCluster controller, the 8 component\n  controllers, and the DSCInitialization controller.\n- Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with\n  correct values in the error logs of all 15 action files.\n- A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster,\n  DSCInitialization) emit `name` and `resourceKind` without a spurious\n  namespace value.\n- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error shows\n  the structured fields present and the message text updated, and the\n  production log consumer ingests both the old and new formats without\n  configuration changes.\n- The SRE/Support-identified inventory of text-based alert rules affected by\n  changed message strings is documented and the affected rules are updated.\n- A release-notes entry covering the DSCI key-name migration, including\n  before/after query examples, exists and targets a single release.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or\n  namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs\n  (`name`, `namespace`) — manager binary scope.\n- [P0] DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names (`Request.Name`,\n  `DSCInitialization`) to camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`).\n- [P0] All service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator,\n  Setup) reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` as a structured field.\n- [P0] All action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`\n  as structured fields across all 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC +\n  3 module action files).\n- [P0] Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and\n  `resourceKind` as structured fields (8 module handlers).\n- [P1] DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include\n  `resourceKind` for cross-controller queryability (bundled here because it\n  edits the same log call sites as the P0 conversions; not independently\n  deferrable).\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- Inconsistent adoption across the many controller tiers and action files is\n  the primary execution risk; mitigated by the grep-driven audit checklist and\n  the CI lint rule added in this epic.\n- Log consumer regression and DSCI query breakage are mitigated by the\n  backwards-compatibility and release-notes acceptance criteria above.\n- The open question on the actual percentage of embedded-identity log calls is\n  resolved by the audit in scope; the conversion approach is unchanged either\n  way.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65113,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac712f216ff0358d","agent_id":"a4fb989e24f2e722c","session_id":"c024f609-bb75-4102-a6f5-d71433960ced","uuid":"fb9f4790-335c-4242-b45e-6d6a45d0ceeb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:18:32.081Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
