{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba6b5a6a61d773d0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-8010\n3\tscore: 12\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: critical\n8\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n9\t  description: 'Missing DAG edge for a cross-epic artifact dependency: E001 creates\n10\t    the repository CI lint rule (initially covering manager binary paths) while E002\n11\t    scope says it will extend that same rule to cover cloudmanager paths and its ACs\n12\t    require the rule to cover cloudmanager paths — yet E001 and E002 are declared\n13\t    strictly parallel with no edge. Restructure so the lint rule is not a cross-epic\n14\t    artifact (each epic owns lint coverage for its own paths, or one epic creates\n15\t    the rule covering both binaries) rather than adding a serializing E001→E002 dependencies\n16\t    edge.'\n17\t- severity: minor\n18\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n19\t  description: E001 architecture_claims rationale and the decomposition summary claim\n20\t    the architecture context corroborates the five-controller-tier structure, but\n21\t    the actual context doc (rhoai-3.6-ea.1/rhods-operator.md) describes three controller\n22\t    tiers and does not mention the module controller; the five-tier structure rests\n23\t    on SME input alone. Signal value remains defensible; the rationale overstates\n24\t    the corroboration.\n25\t- severity: minor\n26\t  criterion: Completeness\n27\t  description: Strategy Supporting Documentation lists a pre-implementation Design\n28\t    doc (three-problem diagnosis, before/after examples, DSCI migration guide) as\n29\t    to-be-created; the decomposition folds this content into E003 post-implementation\n30\t    contribution guideline without recording the disposition of the design-doc deliverable.\n31\terror: null\n32\t---\n33\t## Review Summary\n34\t\n35\tScore: 12/14 — fail\n36\tRecommendation: