{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86084a9b23e26f0d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tConverts reconciliation error logging throughout the rhods-operator manager\n35\tbinary from message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs.\n36\tEvery reconciliation error log that currently embeds a resource name or\n37\tnamespace in its message string (e.g. `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile\n38\tDashboard 'example' in namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")`) is converted to\n39\tstructured fields (`log.Error(err, \"reconciliation failed\", \"name\",\n40\tdashboard.Name, \"namespace\", dashboard.Namespace, \"resourceKind\", \"Dashboard\")`).\n41\tThe epic also migrates the DSCInitialization controller off its non-standard\n42\tkey names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) onto the camelCase convention,\n43\tadds `resourceKind` across all controller tiers, and adds a CI lint rule so\n44\tnon-compliant log calls cannot be reintroduced. On completion, operators can\n45\tquery rhods-operator manager error logs by resource name, namespace, and kind\n46\twithout parsing message text.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in manager-binary reconciliation error\n51\t  paths and produce a per-tier coverage checklist (confirming the estimated\n52\t  ~75% of calls that embed resource identity in message strings).\n53\t- Convert every reconciliation error log in the manager binary that embeds\n54\t  resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value\n55\t  pairs using `name` and `namespace`.\n56\t- Migrate the DSCInitialization controller from the non-standard key names\n57\t  `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` to `name` and `namespace`.\n58\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in:\n59\t  - the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator,\n60\t    Setup), where the kind is not implied by the controller name;\n61\t  - the module controller and its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway,\n62\t    KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator);\n63\t  - the DataScienceCluster controller and the 8 component controllers\n64\t    (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer,\n65\t    TrainingOperator, TrustyAI) for cross-controller queryability;\n66\t  - the DSCInitialization controller.\n67\t- Apply `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` to error logs in all 15 action\n68\t  files across the four tiers: 8 component action files\n69\t  (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files\n70\t  (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action\n71\t  file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and 3\n72\t  module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n73\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization)\n74\t  correctly: `name` and `resourceKind` present, `namespace` omitted or empty —\n75\t  never a spurious value.\n76\t- Add a CI lint/static-analysis rule to the repository that flags `log.Error`\n77\t  calls embedding resource identity in message text or missing the required\n78\t  structured fields, initially covering the manager binary paths.\n79\t- Verify backwards compatibility: before/after log output comparison for a\n80\t  sample reconciliation error; confirm the log consumer stack (Loki) ingests\n81\t  both formats without configuration changes; coordinate with SRE/Support to\n82\t  identify and update text-based alert rules that rely on changed message\n83\t  strings.\n84\t- Document the DSCI key-name migration in release notes with before/after\n85\t  query examples, targeted at a single release transition.\n86\t\n87\t## Acceptance Criteria\n88\t\n89\t- Static analysis over the manager binary reports zero reconciliation-error\n90\t  `log.Error` calls that embed resource name or namespace in the message text,\n91\t  and the CI lint rule flags a deliberately non-compliant sample call in a test.\n92\t- A codebase grep confirms no remaining `Request.Name` or `DSCInitialization`\n93\t  structured key names in the DSCInitialization controller, and a unit test\n94\t  asserting DSCI error logs contain `name` and `namespace` passes.\n95\t- Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with\n96\t  the correct value for all 5 service controllers, the module controller and\n97\t  its 8 module handlers, the DataScienceCluster controller, the 8 component\n98\t  controllers, and the DSCInitialization controller.\n99\t- Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with\n100\t  correct values in the error logs of all 15 action files.\n101\t- A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster,\n102\t  DSCInitialization) emit `name` and `resourceKind` without a spurious\n103\t  namespace value.\n104\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error shows\n105\t  the structured fields present and the message text updated, and the\n106\t  production log consumer ingests both the old and new formats without\n107\t  configuration changes.\n108\t- The SRE/Support-identified inventory of text-based alert rules affected by\n109\t  changed message strings is documented and the affected rules are updated.\n110\t- A release-notes entry covering the DSCI key-name migration, including\n111\t  before/after query examples, exists and targets a single release.\n112\t\n113\t## HLR Traceability\n114\t\n115\t- [P0] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or\n116\t  namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs\n117\t  (`name`, `namespace`) — manager binary scope.\n118\t- [P0] DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names (`Request.Name`,\n119\t  `DSCInitialization`) to camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`).\n120\t- [P0] All service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator,\n121\t  Setup) reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` as a structured field.\n122\t- [P0] All action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`\n123\t  as structured fields across all 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC +\n124\t  3 module action files).\n125\t- [P0] Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and\n126\t  `resourceKind` as structured fields (8 module handlers).\n127\t- [P1] DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include\n128\t  `resourceKind` for cross-controller queryability (bundled here because it\n129\t  edits the same log call sites as the P0 conversions; not independently\n130\t  deferrable).\n131\t\n132\t## Risks and Notes\n133\t\n134\t- Inconsistent adoption across the many controller tiers and action files is\n135\t  the primary execution risk; mitigated by the grep-driven audit checklist and\n136\t  the CI lint rule added in this epic.\n137\t- Log consumer regression and DSCI query breakage are mitigated by the\n138\t  backwards-compatibility and release-notes acceptance criteria above.\n139\t- The open question on the actual percentage of embedded-identity log calls is\n140\t  resolved by the audit in scope; the conversion approach is unchanged either\n141\t  way.\n142\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b94e76493e74e27","agent_id":"a3a7ee4467d836cab","session_id":"c024f609-bb75-4102-a6f5-d71433960ced","uuid":"306574e7-cecd-479d-ad27-5b025c9ac81b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:25:15.373Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86084a9b23e26f0d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
