{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b59b92f9b6f3e0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Standardize cloudmanager reconciliation error logs with structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize cloudmanager reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tApplies the same structured logging standardization to the cloudmanager binary\n35\tthat ships with the rhods-operator. The cloudmanager binary handles multi-cloud\n36\tinfrastructure dependencies (deployed on AWS EKS, Azure AKS, and CoreWeave) and\n37\treconciles the AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, and\n38\tCoreWeaveKubernetesEngine resources through a shared reconciler pattern that\n39\talready provides `name` and `namespace` via controller-runtime's request logger.\n40\tThis epic converts any remaining message-embedded resource identity in those\n41\tcontrollers' error paths to structured key-value pairs and adds `resourceKind`\n42\tso the infrastructure kinds are queryable like all manager-binary resources.\n43\tThe work is in the same repository as the manager binary changes but is an\n44\tarchitecturally distinct sub-system with a narrower deployment footprint\n45\t(non-OpenShift Kubernetes only), so it is separately schedulable.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Audit `log.Error()` call sites in the reconciliation error paths of the three\n50\t  cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine,\n51\t  CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine).\n52\t- Convert any error log that embeds resource name or namespace in the message\n53\t  string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n54\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all cloudmanager controller\n55\t  reconciliation error logs (the kind is not implied by the shared reconciler\n56\t  pattern, so this is a functional requirement, not just queryability).\n57\t- Handle cluster-scoped infrastructure resources correctly: `name` and\n58\t  `resourceKind` present, `namespace` omitted or empty — never a spurious value.\n59\t- Extend the repository CI lint rule so it also covers the cloudmanager\n60\t  controller paths once they are compliant.\n61\t- Verify backwards compatibility for cloud deployments: before/after log output\n62\t  comparison for a sample reconciliation error and confirmation that the\n63\t  relevant log consumer (e.g. CloudWatch on cloud deployments) ingests both\n64\t  formats without configuration changes.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- Static analysis over the cloudmanager binary reports zero\n69\t  reconciliation-error `log.Error` calls that embed resource name or namespace\n70\t  in the message text.\n71\t- Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `name`, `namespace`, and\n72\t  `resourceKind` are present with correct values in the error logs of all three\n73\t  cloudmanager controllers.\n74\t- A unit test confirms cluster-scoped infrastructure resources emit `name` and\n75\t  `resourceKind` without a spurious namespace value.\n76\t- The repository CI lint rule covers the cloudmanager controller paths and\n77\t  flags a deliberately non-compliant sample call in a test.\n78\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error shows\n79\t  the structured fields present, and the cloud log consumer ingests both the\n80\t  old and new formats without configuration changes.\n81\t\n82\t## HLR Traceability\n83\t\n84\t- [P0] All cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine,\n85\t  CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`,\n86\t  `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n87\t- [P0] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or\n88\t  namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs\n89\t  (`name`, `namespace`) — cloudmanager binary scope.\n90\t\n91\t## Risks and Notes\n92\t\n93\t- Whether this work ships in the same release as the manager binary changes or\n94\t  in a subsequent release is an open product decision; the epic is deliberately\n95\t  independent so it can be scheduled either way without affecting the manager\n96\t  work.\n97\t- Cloudmanager is only deployed on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure\n98\t  AKS, CoreWeave), so its log-consumer regression surface is narrower than the\n99\t  manager binary's.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b94e76493e74e27","agent_id":"a3a7ee4467d836cab","session_id":"c024f609-bb75-4102-a6f5-d71433960ced","uuid":"981b3775-265f-46ed-8b62-de5576ed2ae7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:25:16.080Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b59b92f9b6f3e0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
