{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8737336f045aecc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Document and publish the structured log field convention\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: 0\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: 0\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 4\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Document and publish the structured log field convention\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tAuthors and publishes the structured log field convention implemented across\n36\tthe rhods-operator's manager and cloudmanager binaries: a contribution\n37\tguideline for new controller development in the rhods-operator repository, plus\n38\tpublication of the convention for external operator adoption. The guideline\n39\tspecifies the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`),\n40\tthe camelCase naming rationale, the three-problem diagnosis that motivated the\n41\twork (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing\n42\t`resourceKind`), before/after code examples drawn from the actual conversions,\n43\tand a DSCI key-migration guide with before/after query examples. This epic\n44\tdepends on the completed log standardization changes in both operator binaries,\n45\tbecause the guideline documents what was actually built. It is a Red Hat docs\n46\tcontent deliverable using the docs-authoring process.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Author a contribution guideline in the rhods-operator repository covering:\n51\t  - the required structured fields for reconciliation error logs (`name`,\n52\t    `namespace`, `resourceKind`) and when each applies (including\n53\t    cluster-scoped resources, where `namespace` is omitted or empty);\n54\t  - the camelCase naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's\n55\t    structured log key conventions);\n56\t  - the three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded identity, DSCI non-standard\n57\t    key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and missing `resourceKind`;\n58\t  - before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to\n59\t    structured key-value pairs, drawn from the implemented conversions;\n60\t  - a DSCI key-name migration guide with before/after Loki/CloudWatch query\n61\t    examples for operators with existing queries on the old field names.\n62\t- Record the explicit disposition of the open question on additional convention\n63\t  fields beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` (e.g. reconciliation attempt\n64\t  count, error category): document them as deferred/extension points with the\n65\t  log-volume trade-off rationale rather than leaving the question unaddressed.\n66\t- Publish the convention as a specification for voluntary adoption by external\n67\t  operator teams, specifically the Cluster Observability Operator team's Loki\n68\t  Operator and Tempo Operator, per platform policy overlay 0008 (RHOAI does not\n69\t  install, manage, or control external operator dependencies).\n70\t- File tracking issues in the COO (Loki/Tempo) projects so adoption can be\n71\t  followed up, accepting that external adoption is best-effort.\n72\t\n73\t## Acceptance Criteria\n74\t\n75\t- The contribution guideline exists in the rhods-operator repository and\n76\t  specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the\n77\t  camelCase naming rationale, the three-problem diagnosis, before/after code\n78\t  examples, and the DSCI key-migration guide with query examples.\n79\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented structured\n80\t  logging changes in both operator binaries, and the review is documented.\n81\t- The guideline explicitly records the disposition of additional convention\n82\t  fields (deferred/extension, with log-volume rationale).\n83\t- The convention is published for external operator adoption, and tracking\n84\t  issues are filed in the COO (Loki/Tempo) projects.\n85\t\n86\t## HLR Traceability\n87\t\n88\t- [P1] Document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller\n89\t  development and publish for external operator adoption.\n90\t\n91\t## Risks and Notes\n92\t\n93\t- External operator adoption timing is unknown and outside RHOAI control per\n94\t  platform policy overlay 0008; publication and tracking issues are the\n95\t  deliverable, and adoption itself is voluntary — it gates nothing in this\n96\t  strategy.\n97\t- The open question on additional fields (reconciliation attempt count, error\n98\t  category) is owned by PM / the Observability team; this epic documents the\n99\t  required-field set per the strategy's HLRs and records the additional-fields\n100\t  decision as explicitly deferred rather than resolving it.\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b94e76493e74e27","agent_id":"a3a7ee4467d836cab","session_id":"c024f609-bb75-4102-a6f5-d71433960ced","uuid":"a2d006bd-5f36-4621-8a06-41a98f563f8f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:25:16.755Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8737336f045aecc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
