{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbf6c32ce6d30b68","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tConverts reconciliation error logging throughout the rhods-operator manager\n35\tbinary from message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs.\n36\tEvery reconciliation error log that currently embeds a resource name or\n37\tnamespace in its message string (e.g. `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile\n38\tDashboard 'example' in namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")`) is converted to\n39\tstructured fields (`log.Error(err, \"reconciliation failed\", \"name\",\n40\tdashboard.Name, \"namespace\", dashboard.Namespace, \"resourceKind\", \"Dashboard\")`).\n41\tThe epic also migrates the DSCInitialization controller off its non-standard\n42\tkey names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) onto the camelCase convention,\n43\tadds `resourceKind` across all controller tiers, and adds CI lint coverage for\n44\tthe manager binary paths so non-compliant log calls cannot be reintroduced. On completion, operators can\n45\tquery rhods-operator manager error logs by resource name, namespace, and kind\n46\twithout parsing message text.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in manager-binary reconciliation error\n51\t  paths and produce a per-tier coverage checklist (confirming the estimated\n52\t  ~75% of calls that embed resource identity in message strings).\n53\t- Convert every reconciliation error log in the manager binary that embeds\n54\t  resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value\n55\t  pairs using `name` and `namespace`.\n56\t- Migrate the DSCInitialization controller from the non-standard key names\n57\t  `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` to `name` and `namespace`.\n58\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in:\n59\t  - the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator,\n60\t    Setup), where the kind is not implied by the controller name;\n61\t  - the module controller and its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway,\n62\t    KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator);\n63\t  - the DataScienceCluster controller and the 8 component controllers\n64\t    (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer,\n65\t    TrainingOperator, TrustyAI) for cross-controller queryability;\n66\t  - the DSCInitialization controller.\n67\t- Apply `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` to error logs in all 15 action\n68\t  files across the four tiers: 8 component action files\n69\t  (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files\n70\t  (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action\n71\t  file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and 3\n72\t  module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n73\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization)\n74\t  correctly: `name` and `resourceKind` present, `namespace` omitted or empty —\n75\t  never a spurious value.\n76\t- Add CI lint/static-analysis coverage, owned by this epic, that flags\n77\t  `log.Error` calls in the manager binary paths embedding resource identity in\n78\t  message text or missing the required structured fields. The coverage is\n79\t  scoped to the manager binary paths and lands together with this epic's\n80\t  conversions, so it does not depend on or block the cloudmanager work;\n81\t  cloudmanager path coverage is owned by the cloudmanager epic.\n82\t- Verify backwards compatibility: before/after log output comparison for a\n83\t  sample reconciliation error; confirm the log consumer stack (Loki) ingests\n84\t  both formats without configuration changes; coordinate with SRE/Support to\n85\t  identify and update text-based alert rules that rely on changed message\n86\t  strings.\n87\t- Document the DSCI key-name migration in release notes with before/after\n88\t  query examples, targeted at a single release transition.\n89\t\n90\t## Acceptance Criteria\n91\t\n92\t- Static analysis over the manager binary reports zero reconciliation-error\n93\t  `log.Error` calls that embed resource name or namespace in the message text,\n94\t  and the manager-path CI lint coverage added by this epic flags a\n95\t  deliberately non-compliant sample call in a test.\n96\t- A codebase grep confirms no remaining `Request.Name` or `DSCInitialization`\n97\t  structured key names in the DSCInitialization controller, and a unit test\n98\t  asserting DSCI error logs contain `name` and `namespace` passes.\n99\t- Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with\n100\t  the correct value for all 5 service controllers, the module controller and\n101\t  its 8 module handlers, the DataScienceCluster controller, the 8 component\n102\t  controllers, and the DSCInitialization controller.\n103\t- Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with\n104\t  correct values in the error logs of all 15 action files.\n105\t- A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster,\n106\t  DSCInitialization) emit `name` and `resourceKind` without a spurious\n107\t  namespace value.\n108\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error shows\n109\t  the structured fields present and the message text updated, and the\n110\t  production log consumer ingests both the old and new formats without\n111\t  configuration changes.\n112\t- The SRE/Support-identified inventory of text-based alert rules affected by\n113\t  changed message strings is documented and the affected rules are updated.\n114\t- A release-notes entry covering the DSCI key-name migration, including\n115\t  before/after query examples, exists and targets a single release.\n116\t\n117\t## HLR Traceability\n118\t\n119\t- [P0] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or\n120\t  namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs\n121\t  (`name`, `namespace`) — manager binary scope.\n122\t- [P0] DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names (`Request.Name`,\n123\t  `DSCInitialization`) to camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`).\n124\t- [P0] All service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator,\n125\t  Setup) reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` as a structured field.\n126\t- [P0] All action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`\n127\t  as structured fields across all 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC +\n128\t  3 module action files).\n129\t- [P0] Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and\n130\t  `resourceKind` as structured fields (8 module handlers).\n131\t- [P1] DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include\n132\t  `resourceKind` for cross-controller queryability (bundled here because it\n133\t  edits the same log call sites as the P0 conversions; not independently\n134\t  deferrable).\n135\t\n136\t## Risks and Notes\n137\t\n138\t- Inconsistent adoption across the many controller tiers and action files is\n139\t  the primary execution risk; mitigated by the grep-driven audit checklist and\n140\t  the CI lint coverage added in this epic.\n141\t- Log consumer regression and DSCI query breakage are mitigated by the\n142\t  backwards-compatibility and release-notes acceptance criteria above.\n143\t- The open question on the actual percentage of embedded-identity log calls is\n144\t  resolved by the audit in scope; the conversion approach is unchanged either\n145\t  way.\n146\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c8744d23dc4db6f","agent_id":"a6df8657a966d6df5","session_id":"c024f609-bb75-4102-a6f5-d71433960ced","uuid":"75bc05bc-73eb-4305-b66c-aad22aa08c9c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:27:28.877Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbf6c32ce6d30b68","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
